There's not a great way to do this right now, the easiest would be to make a custom output binding <http://rstudio.github.io/shiny/tutorial/#building-outputs> that looks like textOutputBinding <https://github.com/rstudio/shiny/blob/0c19105fbfddf7c5ea3948c6374e16757bcf2253/inst/www/shared/shiny.js#L970> but overrides the showProgress method. Now to actually update the % completion of the progress bar, you need the not-yet-documented session$sendJavascript or session$sendCustomMessage features; there are examples in Winston's testapp repository <https://github.com/wch/testapp>; see the message-handler folders and sendjs as well.

In the future we hope to be able to provide better progress indicator APIs and widgets right in the framework.

