Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/shiny-discuss/c/RYWFJzv9nUE/m/9_qLim3HlysJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I'm using javascript to modify my shiny page. I wrote a small script to listen to the shiny websocket. By using this you can listen to events which would normally be hidden. Maybe its useful for you!

window.Shiny.shinyapp.$socket.onmessage = function(e) {
//trigger R event op the body en send data from R with the event
  $('body').trigger('R', $.parseJSON(e.data));
//you need this line to not break shiny internally
window.Shiny.shinyapp.dispatchMessage(e.data);
}
$('body').on('R', function(event, data) {

//for some insight in incoming data
console.log('R-data-recieved', data);
});

