Dear Joe,

 How to include several tags$video in renderUI() ? As shown in the wikipedia example <http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HTML5_video#.3Cvideo.3E_element_examples> we must include the video in several formats if we want multi-browsers compatibility. But they must be included in a unique <video>...</video> container.

Le jeudi 30 mai 2013 18:42:20 UTC+2, Joe Cheng [RStudio] a écrit :
> I think you want to write the video file into a subdirectory of your app called "www" (if it doesn't have one, create one). The name of the subdirectory MUST be "www".
>
> Then use renderUI instead of renderImage. Your renderUI block should return a video tag like so:
>
> tags$video(src=filename, width="640", height="480")
>
