I talked to Alex in person about this, but for anyone who is curious, something like option 2 makes a lot more sense to me given the reactive primitives we have today:

values <- reactiveValues()
parallelGet(input$url, function(result) {
  values$data <- result
})

output$foo <- renderPlot({ plot(values$data) })

On Fri, May 31, 2013 at 12:07 AM, Alex Brown <alexb...@gmail.com> wrote:

> I'm looking at http://www.omegahat.org/RCurl/xmlParse.html and working out how to make it a nice neighbour to shiny.
>
> Models:
>
> 1) a function - as above
> 2) a special reactiveValue with a mechanism to specify (and update) the URL for each value

